  {
   "id": "small",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: small and simple first-level caches. Why is L1 so small, when L2 and L3 are huge?"
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 8: small and simple L1"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "map"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "sm"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A larger cache has longer wires and more rows to decode. Signals take longer to cross it, so the hit is slower."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sm[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "More ways means more tag comparators, and a wider multiplexer to pick the right way. Again slower."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sm[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And a set-associative cache reads every way on each access, then throws most away. That costs energy on every load."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sm[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A direct-mapped cache can send the data on while the tag is still checked. And an index beyond the page offset must wait for address translation."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sm[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sm[4]",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So the L1 must hit in one to four cycles at full clock speed."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "sm"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "smm"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "smm[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "It stays small, typically 32 to 64 kilobytes, with size divided by ways no larger than a page. The growth goes into L2 and L3, which can afford a slower hit."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "smm[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "smm[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "smm[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "smm[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "L1: fast and lean · capacity goes to L2 and L3"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "waypred",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: way prediction. Can we get the miss rate of a 4-way cache with the hit time of a direct-mapped one?"
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 8: way prediction"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "smm"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "wp"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Each set keeps a few extra bits that predict which way the next access will hit. Only that way's tag is compared first."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "wp[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "An access to tag hex 3 C. The predictor says way 2."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "wp[2][2]",
       "value": "predicted",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "wp[2]",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Way 2 holds 3 C. Prediction right: the data comes out in one cycle, just like a direct-mapped cache."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "wp[2][2]",
       "value": "predicted: hit"
      },
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "wp[2][1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "wp[4][2]",
       "value": "1 cycle",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Next, tag hex 0 7. The predictor again says way 2."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "wp[2][3]",
       "value": "predicted",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "wp[2]",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Wrong. The other ways are checked in the next cycle, the hit is found in way 1, and the predictor is updated. The hit took 2 cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "wp[2][3]",
       "value": "predicted: no"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "wp[1][3]",
       "value": "next cycle: hit",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "wp[1]",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "wp[4][3]",
       "value": "2 cycles",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Predictions are right more than 90 percent of the time for 2-way caches, and about 80 percent for 4-way. With 85 percent right, the average hit time is 0.85 times 1, plus 0.15 times 2: 1.15 cycles."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "wp"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "wpm"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "wpm[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Compare three caches with a 25 cycle miss penalty. Direct-mapped: hit 1, miss rate 5 percent. AMAT 2.25."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "wpm[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "wpm[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A plain 4-way cache misses less, 4 percent, but its hit takes 1.3 cycles. AMAT 2.3: no better."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "wpm[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "wpm[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The 4-way with prediction keeps the 4 percent miss rate with a 1.15 cycle hit. AMAT 2.15, the best of the three."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "wpm[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "wpm[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A variant called way selection reads only the predicted way's data too. That saves most of the energy of a set-associative read."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "way prediction: the miss rate of N ways, nearly the hit time of 1 way"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "banks",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: two ways to raise bandwidth. First, pipelined cache access."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 8: pipelined and multibanked caches"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "wpm"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "pa"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Split the hit into stages, so a new access can start every cycle and the clock can be faster. On Intel, the L1 instruction cache hit took 1 cycle on the Pentium, 2 on the Pentium Pro to Pentium III, and 4 on the Pentium 4 and Core i7."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pa[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pa[1]",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pa[2]",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The price: a load needs more cycles before its value can be used, and a mispredicted branch waits longer for new instructions."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "pipelining: one access per cycle, but more cycles per hit"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Second, multiple banks. Instead of one big array, the cache is split into banks that work independently."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "pa"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "bk"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Sequential interleaving spreads blocks across banks in turn, wrapping around. So the bank is the block address mod the number of banks."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "bk[0]"
      },
